## The Pipeline

Modern x86 cores (Intel Golden Cove, AMD Zen 4/5, Apple Firestorm, ARM Neoverse) are wide superscalar out-of-order machines. Typical widths: 6-8 wide decode/rename, 8-12 execution ports.

**Front End:**
- Instruction fetch: fetch 16-32 bytes per cycle from L1I
- Branch prediction happens at fetch time
- x86: decode complex CISC into micro-ops (μops). Decoders: e.g., 4 simple +TUNE decode: 320 tokens in 403.937s
